# Git workflow

`dev` is the default branch and the base for every pull request. `main` is the release branch: never commit on it, push work to it or open a pull request against it. It must never be ahead of `dev`.

Do each change in a worktree branched from `origin/dev`, and bring it up to date by merging `origin/dev`, never `main`. Open a pull request into `dev`.

A release fast-forwards `main` to a `dev` commit that passed CI (`git push origin origin/dev:main`), then tags it. If `main` is protected and needs a pull request, merge the release PR, then immediately merge `main` back into `dev`.

```bash
git fetch origin
git worktree add ../argus-curator-<topic> -b <topic> origin/dev
```

Do not force-push `main`. Do not commit secrets.
